Z||000000||DaveL||09-04-2001||03:49 PM||||A few months ago, my 87 SE 2.5 threw a rod or something equally not good. At any rate, I have a chance to buy a 2.5 from a Chevy Celebrity I think, also an 87. The VIN letter for the engine is R, same as both my Fieros. It only has 44,000 some odd miles on it and runs great. By great I mean QUIET!! Will this motor work? $300 is hard to pass up. Next question is what can I do before swapping out the engine, as long as it's already out of the car? I figure to put in new oil pan, intake, exhaust manifold gaskets, maybe rear main seal, and water pump too. I know I'm leaving some things out...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||09-04-2001||06:12 PM||||That will go right on after you change some on the front for the fiero.<BR>Don't forget to put in a new oil pump since you are going to remove the pan!<BR>Timing componets?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-04-2001||08:23 PM||||replace the oilpump, the cam gear set, and if it's still available install a new crank damper. The GM number I have for that is 10101369. These motors didn't originally come with one. just a solid crank pulley. GM says it will reduce crank vibration and thus timing gear wear.<P>You'll need to change most of the puleys on the motor and most brackets. You should probably replace the belt tensioner rather than move it to the new motor. ||||reg||1
